# These files run inside Linux containers — always check out with LF endings,
# even on Windows, so shell scripts and configs don't break with CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
*.env text eol=lf
*.env.example text eol=lf

# PRIVATE — must NOT ship in the public open-source snapshot. `export-ignore` drops
# these from `git archive`; whoever cuts the release must also exclude them if using
# any other mechanism. The authoritative rationale (belongs / excluded / scrub-first)
# is docs/open-source-manifest.md (§B). Keep this list in sync with it.

# -- Live provisioning/credential runbooks --
docs/web-app-chat-provisioning.md export-ignore
docs/todo-24-secrets-resync-runbook.md export-ignore

# -- Internal ops + working notes (backlog, weekly reviews, agent notes) --
# todos.md exposes the private product portfolio + live provisioning state; it was
# shipping in the archive until 2026-07-22. The manifest describes the exclusion
# strategy itself; CLAUDE.md is internal working notes (IPs/hosts/sibling repos).
todos.md export-ignore
# intake.md is the cross-project request queue — it names the private product
# portfolio by repo (example-app, research-app, …) in every heading.
intake.md export-ignore
docs/open-source-manifest.md export-ignore
# (glob — gitattributes splits patterns on spaces, so the literal filename with
#  spaces can't be used; this wildcard uniquely matches the one Week-review file)
docs/Week*Review.md export-ignore
CLAUDE.md export-ignore

# -- Live governance STATE (the METHOD ships; the populated inventory/BOM does not) --
# These enumerate every private product (example-app, research-app, …).
# Publish ai-governance.md + the tooling + a GENERIC example inventory instead.
docs/ai-inventory.yml export-ignore
docs/ai-bom.json export-ignore
docs/ai-bom.md export-ignore

# -- Product-specific PROVISIONING instances (the infra CAPABILITY ships; the
#    per-product instances name the portfolio). A generic provisioner template is
#    the #15b follow-up; adding-an-app.md documents the pattern. See the
#    infra<->project boundary doc §4. (realm-homelab.json's markets-* clients and
#    kb-manifest.json's product source-repo entries are functional and handled by
#    the scrub/#15b, not export-ignore.)
docker/data/postgres/provision-exampleapp.sh export-ignore
docker/data/postgres/provision-research.sh export-ignore
docker/core/keycloak/provision-example-clients.sh export-ignore
docker/core/keycloak/provision-research-client.sh export-ignore

# -- The publish tooling itself (product-map.txt lists the portfolio). Also
#    stripped from history by publish-public.sh; export-ignore covers the archive path. --
publish/** export-ignore
docs/publishing.md export-ignore
docs/ai-inventory.example.yml -export-ignore
